        <mxCell id="note_bg" parent="1" style="rounded=1;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fillColor=#FFFFFF;strokeColor=#999999;fontSize=11;align=center;verticalAlign=middle;rounded=1;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=10;spacingTop=8;fontStyle=2;fontColor=#555555;whiteSpace=wrap;" value="Deliberately NOT using Redis (avoid over-engineering / out-of-scope complexity): • Interview slot booking (the actual commit step) -&gt; handled synchronously by PostgreSQL row lock (SELECT ... FOR UPDATE) + optimistic version column;   the matching-queue above only decides WHICH slot to try first, it never replaces this transaction (Section 6.4) • job_requirement concurrent edit (SM vs Sub-SM) -&gt; optimistic locking on save; needs an immediate success/conflict response, not a background job • Audit log write (audit_logs) -&gt; synchronous interceptor on the request itself; must reflect immediately, so it is not deferred to a background job • No Kafka / SNS-SQS / event-sourcing introduced — current volume (per-store candidate &amp; interview traffic) does not justify it" vertex="1">
          <mxGeometry height="130" width="1570" x="30" y="1400" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
